  "description": "meme-id: the_only_kkk_to_ever_let_black_men_in; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts three women posing together, with overlaid text that reads 'the only kkk to ever let black men in.' This is a hateful meme that uses a racist stereotype by falsely implying that the Ku Klux Klan (KKK) — a historically white supremacist organization — ever allowed Black men into its ranks. The meme is intentionally misleading and offensive, leveraging the KKK's violent and exclusionary history to create a false equivalence or absurdity. It is designed to provoke, mock, or demean Black people by associating them with a symbol of white supremacy, while simultaneously mocking the KKK's own racist ideology. The meme's intent is to spread hate by distorting historical facts and using the KKK as a tool for racial insult, which falls under the category of hateful content targeting Black individuals based on race.",
